Conceitos retirados de Faraway (2006):

Deviance: 
The term deviance is a general measure of fit
The deviance measures how well the model fits in an absolute sense, but it does not tell us how well the model fits in a relative sense.

Null and residual deviance:
Residual deviance is the deviance for the current model while the Null deviance is the deviance for a model with no predictors and just an intercept term.

Degrees of freedom:
The degrees of freedom for a linear model is the number of cases minus the number of coefficients.